There are nice red tomatoes there.
I want some tomatoes.
"What is the price of tomatoes per kilo?" I ask.
"Sixty rupees," he replies.
The price is not high.
"Okay, give me two kilos of tomatoes," I tell him.
The vendor takes good tomatoes.
He puts them on a metal scale.
He weighs the tomatoes.
"There is exactly two kilos," he says.
"How much is it in total?" I ask.
"One hundred and twenty rupees," the vendor says.
I take money from the bag.
I give him one hundred and twenty rupees.
He puts the tomatoes into my cloth bag.
